# Quality Assurance

## Code Quality Checklist

### C# Projects (`src/`)

- [ ] Follows standard C# naming conventions (PascalCase types, camelCase locals)
- [ ] Nullable reference types respected where enabled
- [ ] Domain logic lives in domain layer — not in controllers or infrastructure
- [ ] No secrets or connection strings committed (use configuration / user secrets)

### Integration and Domain Tests

- [ ] xUnit tests pass: `dotnet test`
- [ ] Domain tests exercise aggregate invariants and domain services
- [ ] Integration tests use realistic fixtures (Docker infrastructure when required)
- [ ] Test names describe behaviour (`Should_RejectOrder_When_InsufficientStock`)

## Architecture Checklist

- [ ] Changes respect bounded context boundaries
- [ ] Commands and queries separated (CQRS branches)
- [ ] Cross-context communication uses events or ACL — not direct DB coupling
- [ ] Ubiquitous language matches `docs/01-overview/04-ubiquitous-language.md`

## Documentation Quality

- README and `docs/01-overview/` match actual branch behaviour
- API endpoint changes reflected in overview docs
- Architecture diagrams updated when context boundaries change
